    basic: "If you don't have at least a pair, go 'All for One'. If you have a potential flush/straight draw, go 'One for All'.",
    intermediate: 'Bluffing: Standing pat early can scare opponents into thinking you have a made hand, even if you are holding junk. However, they have many rounds to figure you out.',
    advanced: "Card Counting: Because so many cards are being cycled (draw 5, draw 5...), you can track which cards are unlikely to appear in and your opponents' hands. If many Spades have been discarded, your flush draw is dead.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "The deck disappears fast. If 6 people are playing and 4 draw 'All for One', the deck is half gone in one round.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Don't be afraid to 'All for One' twice in a row if your first exchange is also rubbish.",
      },
